"""CODE final GIM comparator: Q-15 FROZEN (D-70, 2026-09-26), gated on evidence (W-7, R-60).

Purpose
-------
The comparator half of unit `external-products` (SD-E-05; FR-P1-04-18, FR-P1-04-9).
**Q-15 is frozen**: `configs/experiment.yaml: gim_interpolation_rule = "C"` (bilinear
spatial interpolation on consecutive rotated maps, IONEX 1.0 spec, Schaer et al. 1998;
`evidence/DECISIONS.md` D-70). Before D-70 no comparator was generated by this module and
that refusal was the deliverable; NOW a real `generate_comparator` invocation proceeds
past obligation 1, and produces a real value (`compute_comparison`) once obligations 2-3
also pass on REAL (non-injected) evidence with `comparator_inputs` supplied — the gates
below are unchanged in shape, only obligation 1's outcome has changed. Rule "B" (no
rotation correction) is implemented in `compute_comparison` for the labeled Jan-Nov
sensitivity analysis D-70 retains, and is NEVER reachable through the gated
`generate_comparator` path — only rule "C" is. C-01 is labelled GENERATED, NOT TRAINED in
the model/config inventory -- never fitted. CODE final GIM is an evaluation-time-only
comparator, never a model input, and never presumed independent before the
network-overlap audit (project.md Mandated; `gim_network_overlap_flag`'s definition is
D-71: direct receiver-presence in CODE's per-day contributing-station list, NOT
independence -- see `compute_overlap_audit`).

Import boundary: importable ONLY by `scripts/04_build_external_products.py` and modules
under `src/evaluation/` (TE 12; TA-07). `tests/test_iri_denial.py` asserts the boundary
with an `ast` scan and never imports this module; behaviour is exercised through the
allowlisted stage script.

The four obligations (R-60), and where each stands after D-70:

1. the interpolation rule -- ✅ FROZEN (D-70, "C"): a real attempt now proceeds past this
   gate. Obligations 2-3 below still gate whether a value is actually produced;
2. one sample interpolation hand-checked against the code, EV-11 placing the
   hand-calculation BEFORE generation: the hand-check's timestamp is asserted to
   precede generation, and a comparator generated before the hand-check FAILS rather
   than being accepted retrospectively. `compute_comparison`'s rule-"C" output at BSHM,
   2022-04-10 00:20 UTC, has been verified byte-for-byte against
   `evidence/r60_gim_gate_inputs/R60_handcheck_2026-09-26.md`'s worked arithmetic
   (18.333 TECU rule B, 18.262 TECU rule C, both reproduced exactly);
3. the map-product-to-map-product limitation AND the spatial-representativeness
   mismatch are EMITTED BY THE REPORTING PATH ITSELF (`render_comparison_report`) --
   a sentence a human must remember does not survive a new report being added;
4. never tuned and then claimed independent: a PARTIAL control plus a NAMED residual.
   The grep-class check that no fitting, tuning, optimiser or parameter-search call
   appears in this module lives in `tests/test_external_drivers.py`; the report states
   no tuning occurred with the independence claim citing the overlap audit. ⚠ THE
   RESIDUAL, GENUINELY UNCOVERED: tuning performed OUTSIDE this module and its result
   pasted in as a constant is reached by no check and remains a reporting-discipline
   obligation, named here rather than papered over (R-60).

The `gim_network_overlap_flag` disclosure is UNCONDITIONAL and its trigger is the
COMPARISON'S EXISTENCE (Vision 6.10: "No independence claim may be made before that
audit"): emitting, serializing or reporting ANY GIM comparison with no registered
overlap-audit result and its flag value FAILS, and the audit's recorded timestamp must
PRECEDE comparator generation -- the same enforceable shape obligation 2 uses. The
January-November 2022 audit HAS run (D-71): ARUC False, BSHM True, NICO True. December's
status is NOT determined by that audit and is never extrapolated (D-71's own text).

Inputs
------
The Q-15 rule as resolved from the governed experiment config by the orchestrating
stage script (`"C"`, D-70), plus hand-check, overlap-audit, comparison, and (for real
generation) `comparator_inputs` mappings. This module reads no config directly and reads
a file only inside `compute_comparison`/`validate_ionex_file`/`verify_ionex_bundle`,
given an explicit caller-supplied path -- it never discovers or globs for IONEX files
itself.

Re-run behaviour
----------------
Pure functions over arguments and an explicitly-named file; no implicit state. Re-running
with the same inputs and the same file bytes reproduces the same result.
"""

